course: dictionary
lesson: 10279
title: Tore: past tense and fast action
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tore is the past tense of tear, so it tells us something already happened. Today you tear, yesterday you tore, and in the past you have torn. «She tore open the letter.» Tore means she ripped the envelope open.
explain: Tore has more than one meaning. It can mean pulled apart or made a rip, as when a shirt tore on a nail. It can also mean moved very fast and wildly: «the dog tore across the field». Read the words around tore to find which meaning fits.
explain: Tore is also in an old verse from the Bible: «Rend your heart and not your garments». In Bible times, sad people tore their clothes to show sorrow. The verse says God wants the sorrow inside the heart, not only shown by torn clothes. Rend is an old word that means the same as tore.
fact: Tear is the present, tore is the past, and torn comes after has, have or had: «She has torn her coat.»
fact: «Tore» can mean ripped apart, made a hole, or moved very fast.
fact: «Tore up» means ripped into pieces; «tore down» means destroyed a building or pulled something down.
fact: «Tore off» and «tore open» are useful phrases: «He tore off his wet socks.»
fact: Paper and tissue tear easily, while strong materials are much harder to tear.
exercise: «The children tore open the parcel.» What does tore mean here? | Painted over | *Ripped open quickly | Washed clean | Carefully folded up
exercise: Yesterday Sam ___ his jumper on a nail. Which word fits the gap? | torn | tear | tearing | *tore
exercise: «The dog tore across the field.» What does tore suggest? | Walked slowly | Sat down and barked | Slept under a tree | *Ran very fast and wildly
test: Which sentence uses tore correctly as the past of tear? | *Yesterday she tore her map. | Yesterday she has tore her map. | Yesterday she tear her map. | Yesterday she tearing her map.
test: «Tore down» means what? | *Destroyed a building or pulled something down | Built up again | Lit a fire | Cleaned the windows
exam: In the verse «Rend your heart and not your garments», what did sad people in Bible times do to their clothes? | *Tore them | Washed them | Folded them | Ironed them
